  "findings": [
    {
      "end_line": 181,
      "evidence": "preparation_v1 checks completed/config metadata, expected dataset paths and no shadow tokenized file, but never calls bound(value). native_child calls that function at113 and passes prepared_dir/mlm to the unchanged author loader at127\u2013149. The author ARGDataset and model tokenizer directly pickle.load the train/val files. Neither this path nor the root request validator rehashes the consumed raw pickle bytes.",
      "file": "research/reviews/American_C3_native_MLM_full_source_v1/consumer_contract_v1.py",
      "id": "C3-MLM-01",
      "impact": "A changed raw corpus can be consumed while the capability/completion still claim immutable original v3 SHA/count provenance. Closed READONLY authority revokes known future writes, but its scope measurement/metadata receipt does not verify current payload hashes. No observed corruption is alleged.",
      "priority": "P1",
      "remedy": "For the actual full mlm phase, before native author decoding, stream-verify the consumed mlm/train and mlm/val regular files against the exact PREP_REF native_dataset_refs with stable-read identity checks; verify any row-order sidecar if used to certify row identities. Bind the successful byte-verification evidence. Keep the synthetic qualifier free of biological payload reads. Do not substitute/rewrite corpus files or infer exact byte identity from closure metadata alone.",
      "start_line": 175,
      "title": "Full MLM does not verify the consumed corpus bytes against completed v3 refs"
    },
    {
      "end_line": 145,
      "evidence": "proc.wait at134 is followed unconditionally by _signal_group(proc.pid,SIGTERM) at135; group KILL may follow at145. The finally path161\u2013173 and live proc.poll/drain branch also use numeric group signals after poll/wait can reap the leader. _signal_group performs only os.killpg and does not verify PID/start identity or current owned membership.",
      "file": "research/reviews/American_C3_native_MLM_full_source_v1/supervisor_v1.py",
      "id": "C3-MLM-02",
      "impact": "Once the original group disappears, the reaped leader PID/PGID can be reused. A subsequent numeric group signal can target an unrelated newly created group. This is inherited from the frozen loop; AST equality does not qualify ownership safety. No process signaling was performed during review.",
      "priority": "P2",
      "remedy": "Use an ownership-preserving wait/drain design: retain the exact leader identity while group signaling is possible, then reap it and only observe group absence, or signal only verified owned process/start identities after reaping. Do not send blind numeric killpg after ownership can be lost. Preserve genuine direct wait statuses, adopted reaping, complete drain and failure artifacts.",
      "start_line": 134,
      "title": "Inherited inner supervisor signals a numeric PGID after its leader is reaped"
    }
  ],
